module-oss (OSSv4, illumos): monitor name and presence on HDMI/DisplayPort.
A digital device takes the connected monitor's name as its description
("DELL U2713HM" instead of "HDMI / DisplayPort Audio 2"): audiohd puts it
into the device description, so CARDINFO's longname reads
"DisplayPort: DELL U2713HM (a)" or "HDMI: <name> (a)" (several joined with
", "); without a name it is the plain description and nothing changes.
The driver's "hdmi-connected" mixer control (1 = a monitor sensed) sets the
HDMI port's availability, so desktops hide an output without a monitor.
Both are re-read in the existing one-second volume poll, so hot-plugging a
monitor updates them.  With an older audiohd (no hdmi-connected, no names)
availability stays unknown and the numbered description is kept.
OpenIndiana project, 2026.

